  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466390",
      "title": "Setting Up the DataStorage Service",
      "lectureOrder": 605,
      "videoOrder": 557,
      "sourceHash": "8f8119c56869c75d0a774f8197f98766c5b0cd47a111bcc7e78fba975b459149",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.183,
          "end": 4.56,
          "en": "-: (Instructor) To use the Angular HTTP service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.56,
          "end": 6.15,
          "en": "just bring this back in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.15,
          "end": 9.78,
          "en": "I want to use it here to save and fetch recipes in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.78,
          "end": 14.01,
          "en": "So to use that we need a place to make these HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.01,
          "end": 16.29,
          "en": "Now the buttons I just showed you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.29,
          "end": 18.42,
          "en": "can be found in the header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.42,
          "end": 21.54,
          "en": "So there indeed if we have a look at our project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.54,
          "end": 23.13,
          "en": "we have the header component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.13,
          "end": 26.88,
          "en": "Here we have the safe data and the fetch data buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.88,
          "end": 29.13,
          "en": "and there's our header component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.13,
          "end": 31.86,
          "en": "Now of course one thing we could do is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.86,
          "end": 34.32,
          "en": "we could add click listeners to these buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.32,
          "end": 37.2,
          "en": "And then in the component body of the header component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.2,
          "end": 40.71,
          "en": "we could inject the Angular HTTP service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.71,
          "end": 43.32,
          "en": "and make our HTTP requests here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.32,
          "end": 45.78,
          "en": "Now this has a couple of disadvantages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.78,
          "end": 49.74,
          "en": "One disadvantage is that here in the header component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.74,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "we have the buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 54.48,
          "en": "but we don't really have the data we want to interact with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.48,
          "end": 56.07,
          "en": "The data we want to interact with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.07,
          "end": 57.69,
          "en": "are our recipes of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.69,
          "end": 60.75,
          "en": "and these are managed in the recipes service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.75,
          "end": 64.44,
          "en": "Therefore, a better place to make these requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.44,
          "end": 66.57,
          "en": "would be the recipe service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.57,
          "end": 69.06,
          "en": "Though I'll take yet another route here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.06,
          "end": 70.86,
          "en": "which is optional though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 70.86,
          "end": 75.03,
          "en": "I will create a new service for this in the shared folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.03,
          "end": 78.87,
          "en": "And I will name this data dash Storage Service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.87,
          "end": 80.31,
          "en": "and that is totally optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 80.31,
          "end": 83.25,
          "en": "You could definitely manage this in the recipe service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 83.25,
          "end": 84.53999999999999,
          "en": "I just want to split this up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.53999999999999,
          "end": 89.01,
          "en": "to make it really easy to focus on that HTTP functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 89.01,
          "end": 90.84,
          "en": "and for you to quickly find it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.84,
          "end": 93.33,
          "en": "if you later go through that project again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93.33,
          "end": 95.4,
          "en": "But handling the HTTP requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.4,
          "end": 97.97999999999999,
          "en": "in the recipe service would be perfectly fine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.97999999999999,
          "end": 100.95,
          "en": "because we are interacting with recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 100.95,
          "end": 103.71000000000001,
          "en": "Yet here is the data storage service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 103.71000000000001,
          "end": 106.02000000000001,
          "en": "and there let's export a clause",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.02000000000001,
          "end": 108.33,
          "en": "which should be named Data Storage Service to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 108.33,
          "end": 110.78999999999999,
          "en": "use that typical naming pattern.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.78999999999999,
          "end": 112.74000000000001,
          "en": "And we can again provide,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 112.74000000000001,
          "end": 114.72,
          "en": "we have to provide this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 114.72,
          "end": 116.13,
          "en": "Now first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 116.13,
          "end": 120.69,
          "en": "we will inject the Angular HTTP service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 120.69,
          "end": 124.32,
          "en": "And since we will inject a service into a service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 124.32,
          "end": 126.66,
          "en": "we need to add at injectable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.66,
          "end": 128.4,
          "en": "You learn this in the services section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 130.59,
          "en": "and it is important to keep this in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 130.59,
          "end": 133.83,
          "en": "Theoretically at injectable is optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 136.23,
          "en": "You don't need to add it to your services,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 136.23,
          "end": 140.04,
          "en": "but you need to add it as soon as your service gets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 140.04,
          "end": 141.69,
          "en": "a number service injected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 141.69,
          "end": 143.34,
          "en": "Which will be the case here because,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 145.59,
          "en": "I will inject the HTTP service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 145.59,
          "end": 147.93,
          "en": "And in addition to that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 147.93,
          "end": 149.82,
          "en": "here we can now also use that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 149.82,
          "end": 152.73,
          "en": "newer shortcut of providing this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 152.73,
          "end": 155.85,
          "en": "The alternative to adding it to the provider's array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 155.85,
          "end": 157.53,
          "en": "in the app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 157.53,
          "end": 159.15,
          "en": "We can simply add an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 159.15,
          "end": 162.3,
          "en": "which you pass as an argument to add injectable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 162.3,
          "end": 164.37,
          "en": "where we set provided into root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 164.37,
          "end": 166.82999999999998,
          "en": "Now again, as you learn, this is optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 166.82999999999998,
          "end": 168.66,
          "en": "You could not use that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 168.66,
          "end": 171.42000000000002,
          "en": "and instead add the data storage service here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 171.42000000000002,
          "end": 173.34,
          "en": "to providers just as we're doing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 173.34,
          "end": 175.98,
          "en": "with the shopping list service and the recipe service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 175.98,
          "end": 178.95,
          "en": "And on the other hand you could of course also provide these",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 178.95,
          "end": 181.56,
          "en": "services in the same way we're providing this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 181.56,
          "end": 183.66,
          "en": "data storage service now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 183.66,
          "end": 184.77,
          "en": "Now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 184.77,
          "end": 186.21,
          "en": "I already mentioned it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 186.21,
          "end": 188.28,
          "en": "We definitely should inject something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 188.28,
          "end": 190.32,
          "en": "into that data storage service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 190.32,
          "end": 194.55,
          "en": "And that something will be the Angular HTTP client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 194.55,
          "end": 197.7,
          "en": "Now as you learned in that HTTP module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 197.7,
          "end": 199.07999999999998,
          "en": "for that to be usable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 199.07999999999998,
          "end": 201.99,
          "en": "we first of all need to do something in the app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 201.99,
          "end": 205.762,
          "en": "There we need to import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 205.762,
          "end": 208.29,
          "en": "the HTTP client module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 208.29,
          "end": 213.29,
          "en": "from at angular common HTTP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 214.71,
          "end": 217.38,
          "en": "So this import statement needs to be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 217.38,
          "end": 219.6,
          "en": "at the top of the app module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 219.6,
          "end": 222.39,
          "en": "and with that added we have to import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 222.39,
          "end": 224.55,
          "en": "that HTTP client module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 224.55,
          "end": 228.3,
          "en": "So now down there in the imports array of our NG module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 228.3,
          "end": 231.57,
          "en": "here maybe after the reactive forms module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 231.57,
          "end": 235.02,
          "en": "because I like to group all the angular modules together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 235.02,
          "end": 237.48,
          "en": "before our custom modules come.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 237.48,
          "end": 241.11,
          "en": "So here we can now add that HTTP client module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 241.11,
          "end": 245.85,
          "en": "and this is crucial to unlock the HTTP client functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 245.85,
          "end": 247.23,
          "en": "in our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 247.23,
          "end": 248.07,
          "en": "With that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 248.07,
          "end": 250.41,
          "en": "in any part of our application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 250.41,
          "end": 253.11,
          "en": "we can use the Angular HTTP client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 253.11,
          "end": 254.88,
          "en": "which means we can inject it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 254.88,
          "end": 256.11,
          "en": "And that's the next step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 256.11,
          "end": 258.6,
          "en": "Here in the data storage service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 258.6,
          "end": 260.85,
          "en": "I want to send HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 260.85,
          "end": 262.14,
          "en": "And I will do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 262.14,
          "end": 266.43,
          "en": "or we will do that by using the Angular HTTP client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 266.43,
          "end": 270.69,
          "en": "Now with the HTTP client module imported into our project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 270.69,
          "end": 274.59000000000003,
          "en": "we can inject the Angular HTTP client here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 274.59000000000003,
          "end": 277.62,
          "en": "For that we first of all need to import it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 277.62,
          "end": 280.2,
          "en": "Now here it's named HTTP client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 280.2,
          "end": 285.2,
          "en": "and we import it from at Angular slash common slash HTTP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 285.42,
          "end": 290.25,
          "en": "Now I will store it in a private property named HTTP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 290.25,
          "end": 293.34000000000003,
          "en": "And again, this is this type script shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 293.34000000000003,
          "end": 295.98,
          "en": "where by adding an accessor like private",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 295.98,
          "end": 297.39,
          "en": "in front of the argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 297.39,
          "end": 300.81,
          "en": "TypeScript automatically creates a property of the same name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 300.81,
          "end": 303.45,
          "en": "and stores whatever we accept as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 303.45,
          "end": 305.7,
          "en": "here in that property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 305.7,
          "end": 308.58,
          "en": "And for Angular's dependency injection to work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 308.58,
          "end": 310.53,
          "en": "we now have to set the type here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 310.53,
          "end": 313.92,
          "en": "off that injected argument to HTTP client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 313.92,
          "end": 316.05,
          "en": "So what I imported here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 316.05,
          "end": 318.3,
          "en": "Now Angular is able to inject this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 318.3,
          "end": 321.54,
          "en": "also thanks to us unlocking the HTTP client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 321.54,
          "end": 323.4,
          "en": "in the app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 323.4,
          "end": 327.39,
          "en": "And now we can start writing logic to save recipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 327.39,
          "end": 330.573,
          "en": "to our backend and to fetch them from there.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
